  "lez": "v0.3.0 (db66590ab821a4e142c211017a3866d007f6fa77)",
  "notes": [
    "Hand-maintained in SPEL's IDL shape: SPEL has no LEZ v0.3 support. scripts/check-idl.py decodes borsh vectors emitted by the core crate with this file and fails on any drift.",
    "The instruction is a borsh enum: one u8 discriminant, then the args in order.",
    "Every account row selects one shard. shard=self is this program's shard; shard=asset is the native shard (all-zero id) for Asset::Native, the token program's shard for Asset::Token (the sale's or pool's collateral). A signer handle is a signing row with shard=self that the program never writes.",
    "PDAs derive from the program's header account: AccountId::for_public_pda(header, seed). One seed is used as is; several are combined as SHA-256 of their concatenation. Const seeds are zero-padded to 32 bytes.",
    "The Sale layout is the v0.2.4 one with fields appended at the end; account_id fields are the 32 raw bytes.",
    "Refusals are guest panics whose message starts with E<code>:"
  ],
